{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION (2026-09-02): ACCEPT as a small task — but with the SIMPLER \"keepalive between operations\" design, NOT a background progress-gated heartbeat.\n\n== Approved scope ==\nEmit keepalive/liveness output SYNCHRONOUSLY at the natural phase BOUNDARIES of a gate op (between sub-operations), on the main thread, via `logging` to stderr (llm/** is not on the ruff T201 print allowlist). Seams already exist:\n  - llm/workflow/executor.py:641  (per workflow step)\n  - llm/runner.py:296             (per LLM call)\n  - llm/agent_call.py:178,202     (per tool call)\nEach emitted line names the phase just completed / about to start + elapsed seconds.\n\n== Explicitly NOT in scope (rejected as over-engineering) ==\n  - NO background daemon-thread timer.\n  - NO progress-gating / per-phase stall-escalation / health-withdrawal machinery.\n  - NO total-runtime cap (stays compatible with ADR 0089 + the silence-tolerance tests\n    test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism / test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout).\n\n== Why this is sufficient (and arguably better) ==\n  - Progress-linked BY CONSTRUCTION: a line prints only when a phase actually completes, so it\n    can never falsely signal liveness during a hang — synchronous emission cannot mask a stall.\n  - Breaks the reported failure: measured phases were 27s / 40s / ~85s-to-verdict, so the worst-\n    case silent gap becomes the longest SINGLE phase (tens of seconds), never the whole op's\n    ~600s silence that killed the reporting agent.\n\n== Residual (accepted, backstopped) ==\n  A single phase legitimately exceeding the watchdog budget (e.g. one model call >600s) is still\n  silent for that phase. Backstopped by (a) the per-request read timeout httpx.Timeout(cfg.timeout_s)\n  default 600s (structured_run.py:419-427, anthropic_model.py:122 \"never unbounded\"), and\n  (b) the re-scoped AC-2 doc warning below.\n\n== AC-2 re-scope ==\nNot a duration BENCHMARK (docs deliberately decline one, plan-review-gate.md:1420-1424). Instead:\na WARNING in the gate docs that gate ops routinely exceed common 600s supervisor stall budgets\nwhile silent between phases, and how to raise those budgets. Note DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S=600 is\nper-request and the close path can issue many (close_autoresume.py while-loop up to\nverify.auto_resume_max), so worst-case wall clock is a large multiple of that budget.\n\n== Lifecycle ==\nRetype from bug -> task; acceptance criteria name a proving command (a gate invocation on a repo\nwhere the call takes minutes emits >=1 keepalive line well inside a 600s window). Not-a-bug\n(feature-request) per prior RCA, now operator-approved to build."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788381517796261001,"uuid":"444eddd8-7b69-434a-97e9-a372746f49fb"}